Subject: [PATCH] server, win32u, user32, dwmapi: The taskbar's band, and what dwm.exe is told of windows.

Windows keeps the taskbar in a z-order band over program windows
(SetWindowBand). A window in the band lies over every other toplevel
window except its own popups; a window with a caption never goes over
it, topmost or not. Menus, tooltips and full screen popups still can.
The composition list also tells dwm.exe each window's owner, class
atom and band, and the whole client rectangle.

dwmapi writes window attributes (DwmSetWindowAttribute: corner
preference, cloaking, transitions; DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow) and
thumbnails (DwmRegisterThumbnail, DwmUpdateThumbnailProperties,
DwmUnregisterThumbnail, DwmQueryThumbnailSourceSize) into the table
dwm.exe shares (wine/arctic_dwm.h). SetWindowCompositionAttribute hands
the accent policy (the taskbar's acrylic) over the same way.
